# Owner Creation Flow & Telephone Handling — Report

This is a Spring PetClinic REST fork. Base package: `org.springframework.samples.petclinic`. There are **two API versions** (v1 handles owner CRUD/creation; v2 only does paged listing).

## 1. Owner entity + telephone field

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`**
Package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.model`, `@Entity @Table(name = "owners")`, extends `Person`.

Fields: `address`, `city`, `telephone`, `Set<Pet> pets`. The telephone field (lines 46-50):
```java
@Column(name = "telephone")
@NotEmpty
@Digits(fraction = 0, integer = 10)
@Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{10}$", message = "Phone number must be exactly 10 digits")
private String telephone;
```
So at the entity level, telephone must be exactly 10 digits. **There is no normalization inside the entity** — getter/setter are plain (lines 71-77). No `equals/hashCode` on telephone.

Superclass **`Person.java`** (same package) contributes `@NotEmpty firstName` and `@NotEmpty lastName` (lines 32-36); `BaseEntity` provides the `id`.

## 2. REST controller for creating owners (POST)

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**
Package `...rest.controller.v1`. `@RestController @RequestMapping("/api")`, implements generated `OwnersApi`. POST maps to `addOwner` (lines 99-114):
```java
@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
@Override
public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
    HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
    Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
    String telephone = normalizeTelephone(owner.getTelephone());
    if (telephone == null) {
        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
    }
    owner.setTelephone(telephone);
    this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
    OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
        .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
    return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
}
```
- **Validation:** Bean Validation (`@Valid` on the generated `OwnersApi` interface param) triggers `MethodArgumentNotValidException` → 400 via the advice (see §5). Additionally the controller does an explicit telephone normalization check returning **400 BAD_REQUEST** if it does not reduce to 10 digits.
- **Success:** returns **201 CREATED** with a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header and the `OwnerDto` body.
- **No conflict/duplicate handling exists here today.** There is no 409 path in the controller.

Other returns in this file: `listOwners` 404 if empty / 200 (lines 76-87); `getOwner` 404/200 (91-97); `updateOwner` 404/204 (118-130) — note update does **not** normalize telephone; `deleteOwner` 404/204 (135-142).

The dependency is `ClinicService clinicService` injected via constructor (lines 56-72). DTO types: `OwnerFieldsDto` (input), `OwnerDto` (output), from `...rest.dto` (generated from OpenAPI).

**V2 controller** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v2/OwnerRestControllerV2.java` — only implements `listOwnersPage` (paged GET). No creation logic.

## 3. Repository / service layer

**Service interface** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicService.java` — owner methods (lines 56-61):
```java
Owner findOwnerById(int id);
Collection<Owner> findAllOwners();
Page<Owner> findOwners(String lastName, Pageable pageable);
void saveOwner(Owner owner);
void deleteOwner(Owner owner);
Collection<Owner> findOwnerByLastName(String lastName);
```

**Service impl** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java` — `saveOwner` (lines 232-237) simply delegates to `ownerRepository.save(owner)` with **no duplicate/telephone check**. `findOwnerById` at 202-204, `findOwnerByLastName` at 239-243.

**Repository interface** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java` — available query methods (lines 46-84):
```java
Collection<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName);
Page<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName, Pageable pageable);
Owner findById(int id);
void save(Owner owner);
Collection<Owner> findAll();
Page<Owner> findAll(Pageable pageable);
void delete(Owner owner);
```
**There is no `findByTelephone` (or any telephone-based query) anywhere** in the repository layer — confirmed by grep across `src`.

Three profile-based implementations:
- `.../repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java` (`@Profile("spring-data-jpa")`) — Spring Data interface with `@Query` JPQL; queries are by lastName / id / all only.
- `.../repository/jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java` (`@Profile("jpa")`).
- `.../repository/jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java` (`@Profile("jdbc")`) — raw SQL; all owner SELECTs are by last_name / id / all. Telephone appears only as a selected/updated column, never a filter.

## 4. Existing telephone normalization logic

The **only** normalization is a private static helper in the V1 controller (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`, lines 217-223):
```java
private static String normalizeTelephone(String telephone) {
    if (telephone == null) {
        return null;
    }
    String digits = telephone.replaceAll("\\D", "");
    return digits.length() == 10 ? digits : null;
}
```
It strips all non-digits and requires exactly 10 digits, else returns `null` (→ 400). It is invoked only in `addOwner`, **not** in `updateOwner`. No shared/util normalization class exists elsewhere.

## 5. How 409 / conflict and other errors are handled

**Global handler** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`, package `...rest.advice`, `@ControllerAdvice`. It returns RFC-7807 `ProblemDetail` bodies. Handlers:
- `AccessDeniedException` → re-thrown so Spring Security yields 403 (lines 85-88).
- `Exception` (catch-all) → **500** (lines 97-104).
- `DataIntegrityViolationException` → **404 NOT_FOUND** (lines 114-125). Note: DB constraint violations currently map to 404, **not** 409.
- `MethodArgumentNotValidException` → **400**, with `title`, `errors` (list of field names), and `schemaValidationErrors[]` populated (lines 134-170).

**There is NO 409/CONFLICT handling anywhere in production code.** No `ResponseStatusException` usage exists in `src` at all (grep confirms). The only `HttpStatus.CONFLICT`-equivalent reference is in tests (see §6). The `ON CONFLICT` hits in `db/postgres/data.sql` are unrelated Postgres upsert syntax for seed data.

## 6. Existing tests for owner creation

Two relevant test files:

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`** — `@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional`, uses `MockMvc` against real repositories. Owner-creation tests:
- `createOwnerSuccess` (lines 102-113): POST valid body → `status().isCreated()`, asserts `Location` header contains `/api/owners/` and `$.firstName`.
- `createOwnerValidationError` (115-126): missing firstName → `status().isBadRequest()`, asserts `$.title == "MethodArgumentNotValidException"` and `$.schemaValidationErrors[0].field` exists.
- `createOwnerMissingAndBlankFieldsListedInErrors` (128-139): asserts `$.errors` contains `firstName`, `address`, `city`.
All use `@WithMockUser(roles = "OWNER_ADMIN")`. Helper `newOwner(...)` sets telephone `"6085551023"`. Assertions use `status().isCreated()` / `isBadRequest()` / `isNotFound()` / `isNoContent()` / `isOk()`.

**Acceptance tests (the 409 driver):**
- **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`** — extends `AcceptanceBase`. `coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone` (lines 10-17) creates an owner, then posts a second owner reusing the same telephone and asserts **`status().isConflict()`** (409). `functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone` (19-23) asserts two distinct-telephone creates both succeed (`is2xxSuccessful`).
- **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`** — abstract base, `@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional @WithMockUser(roles={"OWNER_ADMIN","VET_ADMIN","ADMIN"})`. Provides `ownerNode()` (fully-unique valid owner JSON, lines 117-125), `uniqueTelephone()` = `"04%08d"` i.e. a 10-digit `04`-prefixed number (lines 102-104), `createOwner()` / `createOwnerOk()` helpers posting to `POST /api/owners` (155-162), and `extractId()` which reads `$.id` or falls back to the `Location` header (206-219). The class comment describes an intended telephone-uniqueness rule that normalizes the phone and rejects duplicates.

Note the mismatch that matters for the task: the acceptance test **expects 409** on a duplicate telephone, but the production code currently has **no duplicate detection and no 409 handling** — `saveOwner` just inserts, `DataIntegrityViolationException` would map to 404, and there is no `findByTelephone` query to detect the duplicate pre-insert.

